From 5b4ed5cc7c73ab47f5ce7e823e658bd3aa68a673 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Sun, 1 Nov 2026 17:37:36 +0900
Subject: [PATCH 2/5] feat(4leaf): dice and score read one original UI
 manifest, ready for full extraction

- original/OBS/ui/manifest.js defines window.ORIGINAL_LEAF_UI_FRAMES for
  1171 (D6) and 1167 (score numerals). This interim version is built from
  frames already in the repository (1171: 11 of 28, colour-key corrected;
  1167: 10 of 25). The targeted-extract workflow overwrites it with every
  frame; no code change is needed afterwards.
- dice-fall.js: faces = 1171 frames 0-5 (VERIFIED by pip count); tumble =
  every frame >= 6 in native order (order INFERRED). Old path kept as fallback.
- game.js battle score: digit d = 1167 frame d. 0-7 VERIFIED by eye; 8 and 9
  are INFERRED from the sequence (0-7 in order, small '0'=10, '8'=18) and
  labelled as such when shown.
- index.html loads the manifest; sw.js precaches it.
- Dice/score tests read the manifest instead of hard-coded file paths, so
  they keep checking the real source after the full extraction lands.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_011qw76wwfZ8kaKojeP97FsR
